# Port and NIF: measure the boundary

Sources: [leanHaT](https://leancop.de/leanhat/) and
[nanoCoP-i-HT](https://www.leancop.de/ihat/).

Port isolates SWI in a child process. NIF embeds `libswipl` in the BEAM VM.
Both use the same query API and term encoding. Times include boundary and
Elixir decoding costs; this is a small local comparison, not a solver ranking.

```elixir
project = System.fetch_env!("SWI_ELIXIR_PATH")
Mix.install([{:swi_elixir, path: project}])
Code.require_file(Path.join(project, "examples/showcase.exs"))
prover_sources = [
  {"leanhat.pl", """
  :- module(leanhat, [prove_text/1]).
  :- op(700, xfx, =).
  :- include('#{Path.join(project, "vendor/leanHaT/leanhat_swi.pl")}').
  :- include('#{Path.join(project, "vendor/leanHaT/nanocop_tptp2.pl")}').
  prove_text(Text) :-
      swi_bridge:read_goal(Text, leanhat, Formula, _),
      leancop_equal(Formula, Problem), prove(Problem).
  """},
  {"nanocop.pl", """
  :- module(nanocop, [prove_text/2, prove_text/3]).
  :- op(700, xfx, =).
  :- current_prolog_flag(occurs_check, Flag), nb_setval(nanocop_load_flag, Flag).
  :- include('#{Path.join(project, "vendor/nanoCoP-i-HT/nanocopi20_swi.pl")}').
  :- nb_getval(nanocop_load_flag, Flag), set_prolog_flag(occurs_check, Flag),
     nb_delete(nanocop_load_flag).
  :- include('#{Path.join(project, "vendor/nanoCoP-i-HT/nanocop_tptp2.pl")}').
  :- thread_local lit/4, pathlim/0.
  prove_text(Text, Logic) :- prove_text(Text, Logic, _).
  prove_text(Text, Logic, Proof) :-
      memberchk(Logic, [intu, ht]),
      setup_call_cleanup(
        (current_prolog_flag(occurs_check, Previous), set_prolog_flag(occurs_check, true)),
        (swi_bridge:read_goal(Text, nanocop, Formula, _),
         leancop_equal(Formula, Equal), leancop_intermed(Equal, Logic, Problem),
         prove(Problem, Proof)),
        set_prolog_flag(occurs_check, Previous)).
  """},
  {"prover_showcase.pl", """
  :- module(prover_showcase, [run/7, source/3]).
  :- use_module(library(prolog_wrap)).
  :- use_module(leanhat).
  :- use_module(nanocop).
  core(leanhat, leanhat:prove(_,_,_,_), leanhat:prove/4).
  core(nanocop, nanocop:prove(_,_,_,_,_,_,_,_,_,_), nanocop:prove/10).
  source(Prover, File, Line) :-
      core(Prover, Head, _), clause(Head, _, Ref),
      clause_property(Ref, file(File)), clause_property(Ref, line_count(Line)), !.
  run(Prover, Logic, Text, Result, Calls, Inferences, Proof) :-
      core(Prover, Head, PI),
      setup_call_cleanup(
        (nb_setval(showcase_calls, 0),
         wrap_predicate(Head, showcase, Wrapped,
           (prover_showcase:count, call(Wrapped)))),
        (statistics(inferences, Before),
         (once(search(Prover, Logic, Text, Proof)) -> Result = proved
         ; Result = exhausted, Proof = none),
         statistics(inferences, After), Inferences is After-Before,
         nb_getval(showcase_calls, Calls)),
        (unwrap_predicate(PI, showcase), nb_delete(showcase_calls))).
  count :-
      (nb_current(showcase_calls, N) -> N1 is N+1, nb_setval(showcase_calls, N1) ; true).
  search(leanhat, ht, Text, unavailable) :- leanhat:prove_text(Text).
  search(nanocop, Logic, Text, Proof) :- nanocop:prove_text(Text, Logic, Proof).
  """}
]
load_prolog = fn session ->
  dir = Path.join(System.tmp_dir!(), "prover-showcase-#{:erlang.phash2(prover_sources)}")
  File.mkdir_p!(dir)
  try do
    Enum.each(prover_sources, fn {name, source} ->
      path = Path.join(dir, name)
      File.write!(path, source)
      :ok = SWI.load(session, path)
    end)
  after
    File.rm_rf!(dir)
  end
end
```

## Startup and reuse

The first NIF session initializes the VM-wide SWI runtime; later sessions reuse
it with independent engine resources. A Port session starts a fresh OS process.
Times are microseconds and include the first successful query. The order below
is fixed; results are sensitive to warm caches, scheduling and prior NIF use.
Every cell releases its sessions on failure and reevaluation.

```elixir
for backend <- [:port, :nif], attempt <- 1..3 do
  {us, session} = :timer.tc(fn ->
    {:ok, session} = SWI.start_link(backend: backend)
    session
  end)
  try do
    {query_us, {:ok, true}} = :timer.tc(fn -> SWI.call(session, "true") end)
    {backend, attempt, us + query_us}
  after
    SWI.stop(session)
  end
end
```

## Persistent repeated workloads

The proof workloads reuse notebook 02's formula generators. These calls use
the adapters directly, without its diagnostics or proof-term serialization.
We request one proof and check answer counts on warmup and every measured run.

```elixir
quote_formula = fn formula -> formula |> :json.encode() |> IO.iodata_to_binary() end
chain = quote_formula.(ProverShowcase.chain(4))
pigeon = quote_formula.(ProverShowcase.pigeon(3))
workloads = [
  {"tiny", "true", 1},
  {"100 solutions", "between(1,100,X)", 100},
  {"leanHaT: function chain 4", "once(leanhat:prove_text(#{chain}))", 1},
  {"nanoCoP HT: pigeonhole", "once(nanocop:prove_text(#{pigeon},ht))", 1}
]
for backend <- [:port, :nif] do
  {:ok, session} = SWI.start_link(backend: backend)
  try do
    :ok = load_prolog.(session)
    for {label, goal, expected_count} <- workloads do
      ^expected_count = Enum.count(SWI.query(session, goal, timeout: 5_000))
      samples = for _ <- 1..7 do
        {us, ^expected_count} = :timer.tc(fn ->
          Enum.count(SWI.query(session, goal, timeout: 5_000))
        end)
        us
      end
      {backend, label, median_us: Enum.at(Enum.sort(samples), 3)}
    end
  after
    SWI.stop(session)
  end
end
```

## Timeouts and process isolation

Timeouts are milliseconds per solution pull, excluding consumer time. SWI
alarms interrupt Prolog computation. Port also has an external hard deadline
with a one-second grace period; if that fires, the process is killed and the
next request starts a fresh one. Consulted state must then be loaded again.
NIF cannot safely kill arbitrary native code; use Port for that isolation.
An embedded native crash or `halt/1` can terminate the entire VM. This cell
only calls `halt/1` through Port.

```elixir
for backend <- [:port, :nif] do
  {:ok, session} = SWI.start_link(backend: backend)
  try do
    {:error, :timeout} = SWI.call(session, "repeat,fail", timeout: 50)
    {:ok, true} = SWI.call(session, "true")
    if backend == :port do
      {:error, {:port_exit, 7}} = SWI.call(session, "halt(7)")
      {:ok, true} = SWI.call(session, "true")
    end
    {backend, :timeout_and_recovery_checked}
  after
    SWI.stop(session)
  end
end
```

Run `mix run examples/bench.exs` for startup distributions, median/p95 latency,
RSS snapshots and isolated failure. Notebook results are measured on your
machine at evaluation time; no performance conclusion is hardcoded.
